do you know where we left off on the exo performance docs last night?<｜Assistant｜><think>The user is asking about where we left off on exo performance docs. This is a cross-session question — I should use session_search to find past sessions about exo performance work, and also check the PERFORMANCE_HISTORY.md doc mentioned in my memory (docs/PERFORMANCE_HISTORY.md in the exo project).

Let me search both in parallel: session_search for recent exo performance sessions, and look at the actual docs file. The memory says "STANDING RULE, exo perf work: after EVERY finding/step, update the todo list AND append the finding to docs/PERFORMANCE_HISTORY.md, same turn as the work -- never batch for later."

So the authoritative source is the doc itself. Let me find it. Where is the exo project locally? Probably ~/exo or similar. Let me search for PERFORMANCE_HISTORY.md, and also do session_search.

These are independent calls — batch them.</think>

