</｜DSML｜tool_calls><｜end▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜><tool_result>{"content": "1|#!/bin/bash\n2|\n3|# Standardized Exo Cluster Startup Script\n4|# Usage: ./start_cluster.sh\n5|# Detects the current host and sets up the appropriate environment for the 3-node M4 cluster.\n6|\n7|# ── Tunable defaults (override via environment before running) ──\n8|: \"${EXO_FAST_SYNCH:=1}\"\n9|: \"${EXO_DISABLE_METAL_TIMEOUT:=1}\"\n10|# GPU command buffer queue depth. Lower = more headroom for macOS\n11|# WindowServer to slot 60Hz frames in between our dispatches; saturated\n12|# queue has triggered WindowServer userspace watchdog (40s stuck in\n13|# IOGPUFamily) which kills WindowServer and aborts our runner via the\n14|# Metal completion handler. Default upstream is 10. Forked default 5\n15|# is the first stop on the bisect.\n16|: \"${EXO_MAX_ACTIVE_TASKS:=5}\"\n17|# DSv4 indexer sliding-window. 0 (the model default when this env var is\n18|# unset) makes the indexer attend over the full cumulative pooled —\n19|# decode rate halves by ~20K tokens, memory grows linearly, and the runner\n20|# eventually silent-SIGABRTs around the 12-minute mark on long generations.\n21|# 8192 was the validated \"winning combo\" per the dsv4 sliding-indexer plan.\n22|# Unset by default = model default (0, unbounded lookback). W=8192 caps\n23|# the indexer at ~65K raw tokens of lookback — for Think Max territory\n24|# (200K+ context), the original prompt would fall outside that window.\n25|# Decode rate without bounding takes a hit; recover via lower index_topk.\n26|: \"${EXO_DSV4_INDEXER_WINDOW:=}\"\n27|# index_topk is the sparse top-K width for the DSv4 indexer attention.\n28|# Model documented default = 512. Earlier tuning ran at 192 (validated)\n29|# or 160 (unvalidated speed bet, +7% decode). Reverted to model default\n30|# 2026-05-18 14:20 — user flagged that we'd been comparing perf against\n31|# a quality-compromised config without realizing.\n32|# To override: set EXO_DSV4_INDEX_TOPK in the shell env before launch.\n33|: \"${EXO_DSV4_INDEX_TOPK:=512}\"\n34|# P08 Item 2 (SHIPPED 2026-08-31): exact fused top-k Metal kernel for PREFILL\n35|# chunks (L>16) too. Live A/B (server 'Prefill complete' line, 3 reps/side)\n36|# measured 1.61% prefill-wall gain at 220K ctx (370.22 vs 364.24 tps) and\n37|# 0.11% at 75K -- the win scales with P as the op-level microbench predicted.\n38|# To override (back to argpartition baseline): unset this before launch or set\n39|# EXO_DSV4_EXACT_TOPK_PREFILL=0.\n40|: \"${EXO_DSV4_EXACT_TOPK_PREFILL:=1}\"\n41|# P09 Item 1 (SHIPPED 2026-08-31): per-query-block tiled compressed SDPA.\n42|# Replaces the single fused SDPA call over all keys with per-query-block\n43|# calls over (own local window + all pooled keys), concatenated along the\n44|# query axis, so masked-position FLOPs are NOT computed. Live e2e A/B\n45|# measured +7.20% prefill wall at 220K context (739.47s -> 686.23s OFF\n46|# median, 3 reps/side, ranges disjoint). EXO_DSV4_QUERY_TILED_B = query\n47|# block size; 64 measured best. To disable: set EXO_DSV4_QUERY_TILED_SDPA=0.\n48|: \"${EXO_DSV4_QUERY_TILED_SDPA:=1}\"\n49|: \"${EXO_DSV4_QUERY_TILED_B:=64}\"\n50|# 2026-06-04: libp2p -> zenoh migration (exo #2132) renamed this env var.\n51|# main.py hard-errors if the old EXO_LIBP2P_NAMESPACE is even present.\n52|: \"${EXO_ZENOH_NAMESPACE:=MAC_STUDIO_CLUSTER}\"\n53|: \"${EXO_PP_DRAFT_MODEL=$HOME/.exo/models/mlx-community--Qwen3.5-0.8B-MLX-8bit}\"\n54|# To fully disable ALL speculative decoding (PP-mode DSpark/MTP/chained-MTP/\n55|# classic-draft-model, AND Tensor-mode MTP), set EXO_SPECULATIVE=0. This\n56|# used to require a SEPARATE EXO_PP_SPEC_DISABLE=1 flag (which emptied\n57|# EXO_PP_DRAFT_MODEL and set EXO_SPECULATIVE=0 together) because\n58|# EXO_SPECULATIVE=0 alone did NOT actually disable PP-mode speculation --\n59|# it only gated whether DSv4's own native MTP head got loaded ON TOP of an\n60|# already-active PP-spec session; PP_spec_active itself was driven purely\n61|# by EXO_PP_DRAFT_MODEL being non-empty (its default), independent of\n62|# EXO_SPECULATIVE. Removed 2026-07-26: EXO_SPECULATIVE is now a real\n63|# master switch (batch_generate.py's __post_init__ gates _pp_spec_active\n64|# on `use_speculative and draft_path`, not draft_path alone), so the\n65|# separate disable flag was pure redundancy once that bug was fixed.\n66|# DSv4-Flash sweet spot is 256 (251 tok/s vs 152 at 4096) per\n67|# dsv4_prefill_chunk_size_curve memory. Smaller chunks also produce\n68|# more chunk-boundary cache snapshots, which is what the prefix-cache\n69|# uses to serve mid-prompt partial-prefix hits across requests.\n70|# Lowered 256 -> 128 on 2026-05-11: c=1 100K sweep showed -38% wall and\n71|# +65% prefill tok/s vs 256, decode unchanged, quality (needle-in-haystack)\n72|# preserved. See docs/fork-notes.md \"DSv4 c=1 100K tuning May 11\".\n73|# 2026-06-13: REVERTED to 128. The 256 default was committed off a measurement\n74|# artifact (the prefill harness scraped a stray 'Prefill complete' log line and\n75|# reported a phantom ~317 tok/s). Re-measured with a fixed, wall-cross-checked\n76|# harness: chunk 256 = ~118-172 tok/s (a REGRESSION), chunk 128 + seq-split =\n77|# ~274-288 tok/s (the real, verified win). So 128 stays the default. OPT-4's\n78|# sparse-SDPA tiling code remains (gated, harmless at tile 128) but the 256\n79|# super-chunk is NOT a win on this hardware. Override via env.\n80|# 2026-07-01: RE-RAISED to 256 — the regression above predates PREFILL_\n81|# ARGPARTITION. With argpartition ON (default below), the indexer topk no\n82|# longer argsorts (B,256,P) rows per chunk, which was the L-scaling term that\n83|# made 256 lose. Client-side WALL-CLOCK A/B at 100K ctx (bench/\n84|# ab_probe_tier1.py, time-to-first-token over 76213 real tokens, no log\n85|# scraping): 128 = 289 t/s, 256 = 353 t/s (+22%), 512 = 293 t/s (regression\n86|# — OPT-4 gathered-tensor tiling overhead dominates). Needle + BOS-spam\n87|# gates clean. 512 stays a non-default override.\n88|: \"${EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE:=2048}\"  # validated 2026-07-13 (+7% prefill at all context levels; 4096 breaks quality)\n89|# Context-adaptive prefill chunk sizing (2026-06-21). At LOW context, larger\n90|# chunks (256) amortize the ~390ms per-chunk fixed overhead (43 layers x kernel\n91|# launches x RDMA all_sum x eval x clear_cache) — +39% throughput at 100K. But\n92|# at HIGH context the indexer scores transient (B, H=64, L, P) scales with both\n93|# chunk size L and pooled P, so 256-chunk is -30% at 380K vs 128. The adaptive\n94|# logic in mlx_lm stream_generate starts at EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE (low ctx) and\n95|# shrinks to EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE_HIGH_CTX past EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE_CROSSOVER.\n96|# Defaults: high-ctx unset => fixed step (unchanged behavior). Set both to enable.\n97|: \"${EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE_HIGH_CTX:=}\"\n98|: \"${EXO_PREFILL_STEP_SIZE_CROSSOVER:=}\"\n99|# Clear MLX Metal buffer cache every N prefill chunks (default 1 = every chunk,\n100|# original behavior). Setting N>1 amortizes the allocator release/re-acquire\n101|# overhead across chunks — each clear_cache forces the Metal allocator to drop\n102|# its pooled buffers, which then get re-allocated on the next forward pass.\n103|# At 1024 tokens/chunk across a 500K prefill that's ~500 cycles. N=4 or 8 cuts\n104|# this to ~125 or ~63 cycles. Memory grows by at most (N-1) chunks' worth of\n105|# intermediates between clears (MLX's pool reuses freed buffers). Zero quality\n106|# risk — purely an allocator timing lever.\n107|: \"${EXO_PREFILL_CLEAR_CACHE_INTERVAL:=1}\"\n108|# Balanced causal seq-split (default 1). Interleaves query row assignment\n109|# across nodes so each node's total causal attention FLOPs are balanced\n110|# (~1.67x ratio vs 3.0x for contiguous bands). Eliminates the straggler that\n111|# stalls all_gather waiting for the node with heavier causal work. Zero\n112|# quality risk — bit-identical math. Kill switch: =0 restores contiguous.\n113|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SEQSPLIT_BALANCED:=1}\"\n114|# Sparse SDPA tile size (default 128). Tiles the L dimension of sparse\n115|# attention into chunks of this size to keep the gathered tensor small.\n116|# Set to 0 to disable tiling (one SDPA call per layer — bigger GEMMs,\n117|# fewer dispatches). Test: Fable 5 suggested batching may cut dispatch\n118|# overhead with zero custom Metal.\n119|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SPARSE_SDPA_TILE:=128}\"\n120|# DSv4-Flash seq-split (all_gather batch-safe fix, mlx-lm 8a9cdee).\n121|# Default ON — verified clean quality + throughput at B=2 100K-500K\n122|# (docs/b2-mtp-resolution-2026-06-24.md). Without it, B>1 concurrent\n123|# prefill scrambles streams via the rank-major all_gather reshape.\n124|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SEQ_SPLIT:=1}\"\n125|# Batched prefill across all queued tasks. Default ON 2026-05-08 after Phase 5\n126|# cluster validation: c=2 100K MTP=0 went from 7.7 → 13.0 tok/s/stream (+69%)\n127|# with both streams symmetric (no serialization tax remaining). c=1 path falls\n128|# through the heterogeneity gate untouched. Memory: c2_batched_prefill_results_2026_05_08.md.\n129|: \"${EXO_DSV4_BATCHED_PREFILL:=1}\"\n130|# Rendezvous window: how long the runner waits for additional concurrent\n131|# tasks after the first one arrives, before kicking off prefill. Adds the\n132|# same delay to c=1 first-token. 200ms is the empirically-validated default\n133|# (50ms / 100ms: cross-rank libp2p broadcast jitter caused m4-1 and m4-2\n134|# to rendezvous on different iterations, so agree_on_tasks gated to the\n135|# intersection and batched never fired). Set to 0 to disable rendezvous.\n136|: \"${EXO_BATCHED_PREFILL_RENDEZVOUS_MS:=200}\"\n137|# Optional mlx-lm profiler hook. Comma-separated variants:\n138|#   spans         — per-span wall-time accumulator (was EXO_MINIMAX_TRACE)\n139|#   layer_memory  — per-layer Metal memory snapshots (was EXO_PROFILE_LAYERS;\n140|#                   EXO_PROFILER_LEVEL=2 also snapshots before each layer)\n141|# Unset ⇒ all hook calls in mlx-lm short-circuit to no-ops.\n142|: \"${EXO_PROFILER:=}\"\n143|: \"${EXO_PROFILER_LEVEL:=1}\"\n144|: \"${EXO_MEMORY_PROFILE_PATH:=}\"\n145|: \"${EXO_MEMORY_PROFILE_INTERVAL:=256}\"\n146|: \"${EXO_TRACEMALLOC_PATH:=}\"\n147|: \"${EXO_TRACEMALLOC_INTERVAL:=2000}\"\n148|: \"${EXO_TRACEMALLOC_TOP_N:=20}\"\n149|: \"${EXO_MLX_CLEAR_CACHE_INTERVAL:=0}\"\n150|: \"${EXO_GC_COLLECT_INTERVAL:=0}\"\n151|: \"${EXO_MALLOC_RELIEF_INTERVAL:=0}\"\n152|: \"${EXO_LAYER_EVAL_INTERVAL:=1}\"\n153|: \"${EXO_DRAFT_KV_WINDOW:=4096}\"\n154|: \"${EXO_TURBOQUANT:=}\"\n155|# KV_CACHE_BITS and TURBOQUANT are mutually exclusive — TurboQuant does its own quantization\n156|# Default 0 (bf16 KV, no quantization) — chosen 2026-05-09 for QUALITY safety:\n157|# 4-bit KV introduces quantization noise into cached K/V values; even though\n158|# SDPA scores are computed in higher precision, cached K/V quant errors\n159|# compound across attention. Per `feedback_kv_cache_quality_risk.md`, prod\n160|# deployments must use bf16 KV; the perf delta vs 4-bit is ~4% at c=2 100K\n161|# DSv4 sparse-attention (4-bit faster on bandwidth pressure but quant\n162|# noise hurts accuracy). Override to a positive N only for memory-\n163|# constrained deploys near the 124 GB wired-limit ceiling.\n164|if [ -n \"$EXO_TURBOQUANT\" ]; then\n165|    EXO_KV_CACHE_BITS=\"\"\n166|else\n167|    : \"${EXO_KV_CACHE_BITS:=0}\"\n168|fi\n169|: \"${EXO_COMPUTE_DTYPE:=bf16}\"\n170|# 2-pass SDPA block count override (MLX PR #3455). Empirical sweet-spot\n171|# 88 on MiniMax (+6.5% decode at 50K), but slight regression on DSv4\n172|# (-0.5% across c=1..8) — DSv4's sparse-index compressor attention\n173|# has a different access pattern than MiniMax's full SDPA. Leave unset\n174|# globally; benchmark and override per-model when needed.\n175|: \"${MLX_SDPA_BLOCKS:=}\"\n176|: \"${EXO_SPECULATIVE_GAMMA:=3}\"\n177|# Per-model gamma override for the Qwen3.5-style MTP path (Qwen3.6). Its\n178|# dedicated head is trained with block_size=3, so it sustains a deeper draft\n179|# chain than DSv4's depth-1 head — default γ=3, independent of the DSv4\n180|# EXO_SPECULATIVE_GAMMA above.\n181|# NOTE (2026-08-27): DSv4 default raised 2→3 to match the promoted DSpark MTP\n182|# production baseline (24-run verdict @100K was measured at γ=3; see\n183|# docs/dspark-mtp-production-baseline-2026-08-27.md).\n184|: \"${EXO_QWEN_SPECULATIVE_GAMMA:=3}\"\n185|# Eagle K (MTP top-K soft-emb mixture, K=1 fast-path / K>1 mixture path).\n186|# Promoted to K=8 default 2026-05-24 after the no-renorm fix at\n187|# mtp_module.py:715-729 (commit 2d8d5efc) lifted c=1 100K decode from\n188|# 28.80 ± 0.10 t/s to 29.04 ± 0.07 t/s (+0.83%, Welch t=6.19, p<0.001).\n189|# Quality preserved (needle ✓, BOS=0, bistability=0). See\n190|# .hermes/plans/2026-05-24_w3_K8_norenorm_results.md.\n191|#\n192|# DORMANT IN PRODUCTION (confirmed 2026-08-22, see\n193|# docs/roofline-sanity-check-inputs-confirmed-2026-08-22.md): this tunes\n194|# the classic single-MTP-head chained draft path, which is separate from\n195|# DSpark (see EXO_DSV4_DSPARK above). Live production config runs\n196|# EXO_DSV4_MTP=0 (classic MTP disabled -- DSpark was meant to fully\n197|# replace it, per the comment above EXO_DSV4_DSPARK), so this K value has\n198|# no effect on current decode. Left at its tuned default in case classic\n199|# MTP is ever re-enabled as a DSpark fallback.\n200|: \"${EXO_DSV4_MTP_EAGLE_K:=8}\"\n201|# MTP tie-break losslessness fix: DEFAULT OFF (2026-06-09). This was a BAND-AID\n202|# for an upstream bug that is now fixed at the root, and on the canonical affine\n203|# DeepSeek-V4-Flash checkpoint it CORRUPTS output.\n204|#\n205|# History: the batched L>1 spec-VERIFY forward used to be numerically inaccurate\n206|# (hand-rolled bf16 split-softmax), so its argmax flipped vs a sequential decode\n207|# at tied logits → spurious </think> / degeneration. The tie-break (deterministic\n208|# lowest-id-within-eps on the bonus token, eps=0.5) papered over that on the OLD\n209|# bundled-MTP checkpoint, whose logits were sharp enough (top-2 gap > 0.5) that\n210|# the eps window only ever caught genuine ~1ulp ties.\n211|#\n212|# Two things changed: (1) upstream mlx-lm 491f6fe/5b00004 routes the L>1 verify\n213|# through the accurate fp32 fused sparse SDPA — verify argmax is now bit-faithful\n214|# to a clean reference forward (confirmed cycle-by-cycle via EXO_DSV4_MTP_REFCHECK:\n215|# verify_argmax == reference_argmax every cycle). The flip the tie-break existed\n216|# to fix no longer happens. (2) The canonical affine checkpoint has FLATTER logits\n217|# (observed top-2 gaps 0.375–0.5), so eps=0.5 now captures the true argmax PLUS\n218|# lower-id distractor tokens and the \"pick lowest id\" rule emits the WRONG token\n219|# every cycle (e.g. true argmax 111467 → emitted 68599), cascading into total\n220|# garbage (\"petabits\", Burmese unicode) at 0% draft acceptance.\n221|#\n222|# Root-cause fix = trust the now-accurate verify argmax; leave the tie-break off.\n223|# (If a genuine ~1ulp tie cascade ever resurfaces, re-enable with an eps on the\n224|# order of a bf16 ulp at logit scale, ~1e-2 — NOT 0.5.)\n225|: \"${EXO_DSV4_MTP_TIEBREAK_FIX:=0}\"\n226|: \"${EXO_DSV4_MTP_TIEBREAK_EPS:=0.5}\"\n227|# Greedy accept-rule alignment (2026-07-10): argmax over logsumexp-normalized\n228|# logprobs (the MTP-off generator's rule) instead of raw verify_logits for the\n229|# temp=0 accept/bonus decisions — removes the near-tie trajectory divergence\n230|# between MTP-on and MTP-off (the mismatch the retired tie-break fix papered\n231|# over). Default OFF until the byte-equality gate + DSML battery pass.\n232|: \"${EXO_DSV4_MTP_ACCEPT_LOGPROBS:=1}\"\n233|# Regime-b double-rollback fix (2026-07-10): in the pool-flush rollback path,\n234|# restore snapshotted pools AFTER the blanket trim (the legacy order let\n235|# CacheList.trim re-trim the just-restored pools, corrupting the compressed\n236|# pool by a row on every flush-straddling rejection). Default OFF until the\n237|# byte-equality gate + battery pass.\n238|: \"${EXO_DSV4_POOL_RESTORE_AFTER_TRIM:=1}\"\n239|: \"${EXO_DSV4_POOL_SNAPSHOT_BATCH:=1}\"\n240|# Rowseq per-row decode masks + unified spec-state rollback (2026-07-10):\n241|# with these + POOL_SNAPSHOT_BATCH + ACCEPT_LOGPROBS, the MTP verify cycle\n242|# is bitwise-faithful to sequential decode on the REAL batch cache classes\n243|# (ldiff_cycles 9/9 CLEAN incl. wrapped rings). Default OFF until the\n244|# serving byte-equality gate + battery pass.\n245|: \"${EXO_DSV4_ROWSEQ_ROWMASK:=1}\"\n246|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SPEC_STATE_RESTORE:=1}\"\n247|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SPEC_CACHE_ROLLBACK:=1}\"\n248|: \"${EXO_DSV4_SPEC_CACHE_ROLLBACK_C2:=1}\"\n249|: \"${MLX_GEMV_BATCH_INVARIANT:=1}\"\n250|# Steel-level batch invariance (generalized collapse, M*N tiles, split-K\n251|# off): required before re-enabling spec at c>=2 (kernel layer is proven\n252|# bitexact with it, mlx ac73d0c9) but costs ~5% c=1 decode and the c>=2\n253|# spec corruption ALSO has an unresolved serving-logic component\n254|# (2026-07-11 probe: degens persist on the bitexact build), so keep off\n255|# until that lands. Flip together with EXO_DSV4_MTP_C2_MAX_CTX=0.\n256|# 2026-07-12: default ON — the vec+ROWSDPA=3 champion's identity legs\n257|# (gold gate vs loop and vs MTP-off) were validated with steel-BI=1.\n258|# The ~5% c=1 decode cost noted above is absorbed by the vec win\n259|# (33.7 vs 29.5 net). Set =0 only with EXO_DSV4_VERIFY_ROWSEQ_VEC=0.\n260|: \"${MLX_STEEL_BATCH_INVARIANT:=1}\"\n261|# EXO_DSV4_ROWSEQ_FULLBLOCK / _MOE_PARTS_ROWSEQ: DEFAULT RE-ENABLED\n262|# 2026-08-02 -- CONFIRMED FIX for the DSpark self-doubt-loop bug (see the\n263|# EXO_SPECULATIVE comment below for the full root-cause writeup). Together\n264|# with the already-default EXO_DSV4_VERIFY_ROWSEQ, these make DSpark's (and\n265|# MTP's) L>1 verify forward bitwise-equivalent to L sequential decode\n266|# steps, closing the numerics drift that was letting the model see a\n267|# subtly different view of its own context at self-verification decision\n268|# points. Confirmed live: 2x identical temp=0 reruns of the failing\n269|# math_digit_sum repro converged cleanly (finish_reason=stop, correct\n270|# answer) at both attempts, vs the prior 18-24x repetition that never\n271|# terminated.\n272|#\n273|# 2026-08-04 UPDATE: EXO_DSV4_ROWSEQ_FULLBLOCK_MOE=1 (per-rowing the ENTIRE\n274|# MoE ffn -- gate+switch+shared+combine) was the original fix but its cost\n275|# is real: forcing the expensive expert-gather (switch_mlp) per-row instead\n276|# of batched scales verify-step cost with block_size, capping DSpark's\n277|# throughput at parity with plain sequential decode regardless of draft\n278|# quality (confirmed: raising draft acceptance from ~64% to 85-97% via the\n279|# DSpark native-head fix produced ZERO throughput gain under FULLBLOCK_MOE\n280|# -- see exo-perf-tuning skill). An offline bisect (4300 real captured\n281|# verify-block activations across both nodes, EXO_DSV4_MOE_ISOLATION_DUMP)\n282|# found the numerics divergence lives ONLY in shared_experts -- gate and\n283|# combine are innocent (same ~15.6% divergence rate as fully-batched), and\n284|# critically switch_mlp (the expensive expert-gather) is ALSO innocent (same\n285|# divergence rate batched or not). EXO_DSV4_MOE_PARTS_ROWSEQ=shared alone\n286|# reduces the divergence rate to 0.023% (1/4300, noise-floor) vs 0% for the\n287|# full per-row fix -- confirmed correctness-clean live (math_digit_sum\n288|# repro: finish_reason=stop, correct answer, 0 repetitions; tool-calling\n289|# smoke test: clean). NOTE: this is NOT literally bitwise-lossless like\n290|# FULLBLOCK_MOE=1 was (a 1-in-4300 residual divergence remains, vs 0) --\n291|# if the self-doubt loop or any other verify-drift symptom EVER reappears\n292|# in production, that residual is the first thing to re-audit (bisect\n293|# further within shared_experts' own sub-ops, or fall back to\n294|# FULLBLOCK_MOE=1). Throughput: 27.4