 6.02 tok/s. **Decode on this cluster carries a large,\n7490|uncharacterized boot-to-boot term that prefill does not.** That single contrast\n7491|explains the entire campaign more economically than any code mechanism.\n7492|\n7493|**So the 2x2 collapses.** The \"pure crossover interaction\" required exactly one cell\n7494|(0,0) to be fast. That cell has now been measured twice on identical config: 36.08\n7495|and 30.06. The full observed range for the SAME both-flags-off config is 6.02 tok/s\n7496|— **larger than the entire 3.90 \"effect\"** the campaign was chasing. Every cell in\n7497|the 2x2 was n=1 boot, so every number in it is one draw from a distribution this wide.\n7498|The interaction was an artifact of one lucky boot.\n7499|\n7500|**Consequences, stated plainly rather than softened:**\n7501|1. **The -6.13% decode regression is RETIRED.** It was never code. P06's 34.28 and\n7502|   P12's 32.18 are two draws from a distribution whose observed spread is at least\n7503|   6.02 tok/s. The gap between them is well inside that.\n7504|2. **The two flags are fully exonerated for decode**, which is exactly what the two\n7505|   independent static traces said in §P12-addendum. The traces were right the whole\n7506|   time. The empirical \"tension\" that motivated P13-P15 was measurement noise\n7507|   masquerading as a code effect.\n7508|3. **No mechanism hunt is warranted.** Allocator state, shader-cache residency and\n7509|   accept-rate drift were the three candidates for the \"interaction.\" There is no\n7510|   interaction to explain.\n7511|4. **Every historical single-boot delta in this document is now suspect** — anything\n7512|   smaller than ~6 tok/s of decode measured as one-boot-vs-one-boot is not\n7513|   distinguishable from boot variance. This does not invalidate multi-boot or\n7514|   within-boot A/B results, but it does invalidate the reasoning pattern\n7515|   \"relaunched, measured once, therefore the change did it.\"\n7516|5. The **prefill** decomposition from P14 SURVIVES, because prefill is boot-stable:\n7517|   `QUERY_TILED_SDPA` is worth ~34.8 tok/s of prefill and `EXACT_TOPK_PREFILL` ~4.3,\n7518|   additively. Both flags should STAY ON — they are real prefill wins with no\n7519|   demonstrated decode cost.\n7520|\n7521|**Integrity note — a runner CRASH occurred during this run and was investigated, not\n7522|absorbed.** A first rep1 attempt returned `trustworthy=false` with zero tokens. The\n7523|cause was a genuine runner crash at 23:23:46.6 on **both** nodes:\n7524|`ValueError: [reshape] Cannot reshape array of size 1 into shape (2,1,1,1)`.\n7525|Auto-restart CONFIRMED by PID+lstart, not by \"a process is running\": masters 81596 /\n7526|83149 started 22:54:03/04, while the runner children **95798 / 97433 started\n7527|23:23:50** — 3 s after the crash, 47 min after their parents. Restart sequence\n7528|completed 23:24:32.7. **All three scoring reps ran entirely after that** (first\n7529|scoring prefill completed 23:30:22), verified against server-side `Prefill complete`\n7530|lines matching each artifact's `prompt_tokens` within one token. The invalid attempt\n7531|is the only thing that straddled the restart and it is not in the scored set.\n7532|\n7533|**Honest caveat on P15's own number.** Because the crash preceded all three scoring\n7534|reps, P15's 30.06 was measured on a *restarted* runner rather than a cleanly-booted\n7535|one. So P15's low value has two candidate explanations — ordinary boot variance, or\n7536|post-restart state — and this run cannot separate them. **Both readings refute the\n7537|interaction equally**, and the prefill-stable/decode-unstable contrast holds either\n7538|way, so the conclusions above stand. But P15 should not be cited as a clean estimate\n7539|of the both-flags-off mean; it is one more draw, taken under a known perturbation.\n7540|\n7541|### DEFECT — BatchPoolingCache overlap-carry lists are not resized on batch-width change\n7542|\n7543|Root-caused during P15. **Pre-existing, NOT from the P08/P09 window, NOT masked by\n7544|either flag** — all three were checked explicitly rather than assumed.\n7545|\n7546|**Mechanism.** `mlx_lm/models/cache.py:2050`, in\n7547|`BatchPoolingCache.fetch_overlap_carry`:\n7548|`valid = mx.array(self._overlap_carry_valid).reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)`.\n7549|`_overlap_carry_valid` is a plain Python list sized `[False] * batch_size` at cache\n7550|construction (`cache.py:2029`). `batch_size` here is the *current decode batch width*\n7551|passed down from the compressor (`deepseek_v4.py:3262`). `BatchPoolingCache.extend()`\n7552|(`cache.py:2642`) and `filter()` (`cache.py:2619`) resize\n7553|`remainder / _pool_lengths / _lengths / _processed / _pending_bumps` on mid-decode\n7554|stream admission or removal — but they **never touch `_overlap_carry_valid`,\n7555|`_overlap_kv_carry`, `_overlap_gate_carry`, or `_overlap_windows_this_call`**. Once\n7556|the batch grows past the list length, the next overlap-carry fetch that has a stored\n7557|carry crashes. The leading `2` is the stream count, not the TP world size.\n7558|\n7559|**Provenance: PRE-EXISTING.** The crashing line came from `5e88545` (2026-08-20), and\n7560|`git merge-base --is-ancestor 5e88545 a6eb893` confirms it predates the window start.\n7561|The window `a6eb893..2e2d17d` touches only `deepseek_v4.py` and `utils.py` —\n7562|`git log a6eb893..2e2d17d -- cache.py` is empty. The deployed `mlx_lm` in `.venv` is\n7563|byte-identical to the submodule for `cache.py`, so the git analysis maps to what ran.\n7564|\n7565|**Not flag-related.** The compressor overlap path runs on every forward as a sibling\n7566|sub-op (`deepseek_v4.py:4757-4763`); the query-tiled flag gates only the compressed-\n7567|SDPA output path (`:4481-4505`) and the exact-topk flag only prefill top-k\n7568|(`:4123-4127`). Neither routes into or around `fetch_overlap_carry`. Both-flags-off\n7569|was coincidental to this crash.\n7570|\n7571|**Trigger (medium-high confidence): a mid-decode batch-width change with a persisted\n7572|carry.** Logs show five concurrent command_ids active at crash time, one admitted at\n7573|23:16:24, while `_overlap_carry_valid` was still length 1. P13 never hit it because\n7574|its reps were strictly single-stream, so the batch width never changed. First\n7575|occurrence in all available log history on both nodes — latent, not long-standing-\n7576|silent. Decisive confirmation would be two concurrent 100K requests with one joining\n7577|mid-decode.\n7578|\n7579|**Root-cause fix (dispatched separately):** derive the mask length from the\n7580|authoritative batch state at fetch time rather than trusting a separately-maintained\n7581|list, and resize all four `_overlap_*` structures together in `extend()`/`filter()`.\n7582|A guard that silently returns \"sequence start\" on mismatch would prevent the kill but\n7583|drop a real per-stream carry — that is a mitigation with a correctness cost, not a fix.\n7584|\n7585|### P16 pre-register — characterize between-boot variance (written BEFORE the run)\n7586|\n7587|The campaign's real open question is no longer which flag is guilty. It is: **how\n7588|wide is the decode boot distribution?** Until that is known, no single-boot delta in\n7589|this document can be trusted, including the ones that look clean.\n7590|\n7591|- **Design:** the SHIPPED default config (both flags ON — do not run this on a\n7592|  reverted config; the production default is what needs an error bar), N >= 4\n7593|  independent cold boots, n=3 reps each, nothing else varied. Every boot gets the\n7594|  standard `ps eww` proof on real PIDs.\n7595|- **Primary output:** the between-boot standard deviation of the per-boot decode\n7596|  median, and the within-boot SD for comparison. Report both, plus the ratio.\n7597|- **Pre-registered interpretation:**\n7598|  - between-boot SD **>= 1.5** tok/s → confirms boot variance dominates; every\n7599|    single-boot delta in this document under ~3 tok/s must be re-labelled as\n7600|    unresolved, and all future A/Bs require >= 3 boots per arm.\n7601|  - between-boot SD **< 0.5** tok/s → boot variance is small after all, and the\n7602|    P13-vs-P15 6.02 swing was driven by something specific (most likely the crash/\n7603|    restart state) that must then be identified.\n7604|  - in between → report the number and set the per-arm boot requirement from it\n7605|    directly, rather than picking a story.\n7606|- **Do not re-run any flag A/B until this number exists.** Running more arms at n=1\n7607|  boot would produce more of exactly the artifact that P13-P15 just cost four cluster\n7608|  hours to discover.\n7609|- **Also record per boot:** prefill median (expected stable near 417 on the shipped\n7610|  config — it is the control), whether any runner crash/restart occurred, and the\n7611|  warmup rep's value. P15's warmup came in at 12.00 tok/s, far off every other\n7612|  warmup; warmup behaviour may itself be a boot-state signal worth tracking.\n7613|", "total_lines": 7612, "file_size": 472366, "truncated": false, "is_binary": false, "is_image": false}</tool_result><｜Assistant｜><think>Now I have the full picture. Let me summarize where we left off:

