ility per call. fence=4 keeps the 43-layer chain in\n467|    # ~11 fence segments (vs ~6 at fence=8), enough to push per-cycle\n468|    # stall probability below threshold. Cost: ~0.7 t/s on c=1 (29.7 ->\n469|    # ~29.0) from extra GPU syncs — acceptable to unlock c=2 stability.\n470|    #\n471|    # Set to 1 to revert to per-layer fences (slower but maximally stable).\n472|    # Set to 8 to recover c=1 ceiling at the cost of c=2 bistability.\n473|    # Set to 43 only when running gamma=1 (where the chain depth is harmless).\n474|    : \"${EXO_DSV4_FENCE_EVERY_N_LAYERS:=4}\"\n475|    # Metal command buffer size limit. M4 Max defaults to 50MB, but the\n476|    # DSv4 43-layer B=2 batched prefill forward produces >50MB of intermediate\n477|    # results. The 50MB limit causes mid-forward command buffer flushes that\n478|    # create bimodal stalls (fast chunks 0.77s, slow chunks 2.3s, 3x ratio).\n479|    # Setting 200MB lets the full B=2 forward fit in one command buffer,\n480|    # eliminating the stalls. Measured: B=2 aggregate 317 t/s (was 144 t/s).\n481|    : \"${MLX_MAX_MB_PER_BUFFER:=200}\"\n482|    : \"${MLX_MAX_OPS_PER_BUFFER:=200}\"\n483|    # MTP self-spec gate. DEFAULT FLIPPED TO OFF 2026-07-26 alongside\n484|    # EXO_SPECULATIVE above -- with speculation itself off by default,\n485|    # there is no reason to spend load time/memory attaching heads that\n486|    # will never be used at decode time. Activates when (a) the\n487|    # checkpoint contains mtp.* weights (mlx-community variants strip\n488|    # them; use scripts/patch_dsv4_mtp.py to add them back from\n489|    # upstream) AND (b) EXO_DSV4_MTP is non-zero. Set to 1 (with\n490|    # EXO_SPECULATIVE=1) to re-enable plain single-token MTP -- though\n491|    # per the plan for this cluster, DSpark below is the ONLY intended\n492|    # MTP mechanism; there's no real reason to run plain MTP instead of\n493|    # DSpark once DSpark's bug (see EXO_SPECULATIVE comment above) is\n494|    # fixed, so this 